      "text": "To solve for the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).**\n\n   Let \\( y = f(x) = 3x - 8 \\). To find the inverse, we solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   Add 8 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the inverse function is:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set \\( f(x) \\) equal to \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) and solve for \\( x \\).**\n\n   We need to find \\( x \\) such that:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = f^{-1}(x)\n   \\]\n   Substituting the expressions for \\( f(x) \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides by 3:**\n\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Simplify the left side:\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n\n4. **Isolate \\( x \\) by moving all terms involving \\( x \\) to one side and constant terms to the other side:**\n\n   Subtract \\( x \\) from both sides:\n   \\[\n   9x - x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   8x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n   Add 24 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 8:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\n5. **Verify the solution by substituting \\( x = 4 \\) back into the original functions:**\n\n   Calculate \\( f(4) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(4) = 3(4) - 8 = 12 - 8 = 4\n   \\]\n\n   Calculate \\( f^{-1}(4) \\):\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(4) = \\frac{4 + 8}{3} = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\n   \\]\n\n   Since \\( f(4) = 4 \\) and \\( f^{-1}(4) = 4 \\), the value \\( x = 4 \\) satisfies the equation \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\).\n\nTherefore, the solution is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
