      "text": "To find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\), we start by recalling the definition of the inverse function. If \\( f(x) = y \\), then \\( f^{-1}(y) = x \\). Therefore, \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) implies that \\( x \\) is a fixed point of the function \\( f \\), or equivalently, it satisfies the equation \\( f(x) = x \\).\n\nGiven the function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\), we need to solve the equation:\n\\[ f(x) = x \\]\nSubstituting the expression for \\( f(x) \\), we get:\n\\[ 3x - 8 = x \\]\nTo isolate \\( x \\), we first subtract \\( x \\) from both sides:\n\\[ 3x - x - 8 = 0 \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 2x - 8 = 0 \\]\nNext, we add 8 to both sides:\n\\[ 2x = 8 \\]\nFinally, we divide both sides by 2:\n\\[ x = 4 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).",
